# Everything under ops/ is shipped to the Linux game server and executed there -- the
# shell scripts by their shebang, the unit files by systemd's parser. CRLF breaks both,
# and the failure is obscure (`bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env^M`). Pin them to LF.
#
# Same rule, and same reason, as the foodblog repo.
*.sh            text eol=lf
ops/bin/*       text eol=lf
ops/systemd/*   text eol=lf
ops/etc/*       text eol=lf
*.tf            text eol=lf
*.tftpl         text eol=lf
